# The hardened netlist equals the RTL for all time. From all flops 0, for every input
# sequence on the pins and the three macros' outputs, the 24 outputs and the 276 macro
# inputs agree every cycle. The Makefile proves the miter 0 with ABC scorr + dprove, which
# match flops by function, not name; a retimed flop would not match, and the flow does
# not retime.
#
# Trusted: yosys's Verilog frontend, proc, flatten and memory_map (synthesis uses them
# too); the IHP cell models, each proved equal to its Liberty function in cells.ys; the
# macros as shared cut points; one rising-edge clock (asserted in cut.ys and gate.ys);
# an asynchronous reset acting in the cycle it is asserted, on both sides; timing, which
# is signoff STA's. gold.il recodes the state machines as synthesis does, and step.ys
# proves it equal to the RTL as written. Not covered: power-up states other than all 0.
# Vacuity and teeth: gate.ys and make netlist_equiv_teeth.

read_rtlil gold.il
read_rtlil gate.il
miter -equiv -flatten gold gate miter
hierarchy -top miter
delete t:$scopeinfo
script ../netlist_equiv/aig.ys
# the RTL has no x left after gold.ys and the netlist none at all, so the only inputs are
# the ports and the macros' outputs, never an x made free
select -assert-none t:$anyseq t:$anyconst %u
write_aiger miter.aig
